{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/206857-spirit-of-the-altlantic-ocean","id":206857,"title":"Spirit of the Altlantic Ocean","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-24T03:11:54-07:00","id":206857,"title":"Spirit of the Altlantic Ocean","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> Tomorrow i run a session where my pack of humble Uratha plan to get on a ship and cross the Atlantic Ocean from Boston to Edinburgh.<br /> One would assume that a bunch of Werewolfs are not well received by the spirits of the sea. So the pack has to do something about that before they go on their journey.<br /> My inspiration lost me today, because i am sick. So i need some help with this topic.<br /> How would you present the problem and what kind of ciminage could they offer for save travel? What kinds of powerful monsters would you unleash on your pack in this situation?<br /> And how would you make the spirit of the Atlantic Ocean look like?<br /> I really would appreciate some help.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3549-caliban","name":"Caliban","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T03:27:09-07:00","id":206868,"title":"","content":"I would make it a proper, old-school sea serpent, something that should be coiled around the words &quot;HERE BE DRAGONS&quot;. It's made of foam and flesh,the wreck of a thousand ships weaved into its colossal form. She is a harsh mistress and demands life to travel her magnificent vastness; the only truly deserving chiminage for a turbulent sea is a living sacrifice (if you want to go classic, horses are a greek tradition)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T04:41:36-07:00","id":206922,"title":"","content":"Great Ideas! I will totally use that. Thank you very much for this great inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3549-caliban","name":"Caliban","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T17:26:16-07:00","id":208897,"title":"","content":"Check out lodge of the maelstrom while you're at it. They have an oceanic focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T16:42:08-07:00","id":210645,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, the spirit of the North Atlantic is going to be a huge Jormundgandr-style serpent, or perhaps a Kraken. Oh gods, I just envisioned a titanic octopus with dragon-snake-arms...<br /> I don't know what kind of myths the Inuites or the native Americans have of the sea. Those might also be worth looking up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T17:23:35-07:00","id":210659,"title":"","content":"Or its a giant damn walrus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T05:56:25-07:00","id":211123,"title":"","content":"The Inuit <b>Sedna</b> is the fearsome goddess of the sea in the north.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key"